db/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049981 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186051070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186133841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428679 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428680 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1031 "Double Integrals Over Type II Regions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1033 2152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1034 0.9693814428704701 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050264 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "3ab583b8-5390-5f48-b28b-1a89db70664f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127171 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127171 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127171 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127171 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127171 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127171 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127171 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127171 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186475697 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127171 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "aaffb82d-aaf2-5250-9a3c-7bbffe3194af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127177 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127177 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127177 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127177 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127177 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186475757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127177 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127177 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127177 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186475637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127177 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e5a89205-79ee-5c13-8f8f-8670651a6a33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129011 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7197" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129011 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/1d/1d180fd5de88ebc465df522879142e5a4c5446c758aaccde792092968078c254.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is enclosed by the curves $x=2y^3-2y$ and  $x=y^3-4y,$ and the $y$-axis, as shown in the picture. Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} \\mathrm{d}A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129011 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b4697448-d5f7-59ae-86a1-689ae00ebb73" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129011 #edb/ref 1074 "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/68/6812e8036df171e162bee49d2edcff6d4a742e7bb4f14247713bd2332c64ccc6.png)\n\n \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -2 \\leq y  \\leq 0, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq y^3\\!-\\!4y \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nD_2 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq y  \\leq 1, \\quad 2y^3\\!-\\!2y \\leq x \\leq 0 \\bigg\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{3}-4y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{y}^{3}-2y}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}[x]_{0}^{{y}^{3}-4y}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{2{y}^{3}-2y}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}({y}^{3}-4y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2y-2{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}-2{y}^{2}]}_{-2}^{0}+{[{y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129012 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7198" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129012 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y= 2^x,$ $y=\\sqrt{x}$  and lines $x=0$ and $y=2,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of a function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions.\n\n![](images/b8/b80527fdef6f890581b8f56431e1b72a8f7eae3b41827caa16486ed9f2fd45ea.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129012 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9a106b26-c6fe-5e4b-ae43-9cc02ddb67c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129012 #edb/ref 1074 "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as shown below.  \n\n![](images/93/939e46b3ed4266f3c18d3567f951276e420292781cfc414711c244f453bc4029.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x  \\leq 1, \\quad \\sqrt x \\leq y \\leq 2^x \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nD_2 = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq x  \\leq 4, \\quad \\sqrt x \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{{2}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129013 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7199" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129013 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=2+\\ln x,$  and the lines $y=1$, $x=1,$ and  $x=e,$  as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions.\n\n![](images/4b/4b0dff15fa9fa93ed61183702bff6bb443daf14b0adbf56cf4b97e3bd830ceea.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129013 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "be10aba9-930e-54c3-814d-8d089757affc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129013 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,x={e}^{y-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/22/2228ad860fea1e2c30d20bce749f654da02a97c65fd5e70152a07761e26f3e78.png)\n\n    \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y  \\leq 2, \\quad 1 \\leq x \\leq e \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nD_2 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 2 \\leq y  \\leq 3, \\quad e^{y-2} \\leq x \\leq e\\bigg\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{{e}^{y-2}}^{e}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129192 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129192 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129192 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186268864 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129192 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186268866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129192 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129192 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129192 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129192 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129192 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129192 #edb/ref 1039 "Evaluating a Double Integral Over a Partitioned Region" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129192 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186129011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129192 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "4aa355fd-5d73-5cce-9c76-1edafae19751" #edb/ref 1759218604541