edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186475969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129194 #edb/ref 1039 "Representing a Double Integral as a Repeated Integral Over a Union of Type II Regions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129194 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186129013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129194 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "cb3a9009-1c97-57c1-bc3c-45b318a62b8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129341 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129341 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129341 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129341 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129341 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129341 #edb/ref 1045 "Double Integrals Over Partitioned Regions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129341 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186130075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129341 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129341 #edb/ref 1050 1080.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129341 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "58849859-2309-5910-bd3d-67823d7df3a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129615 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186127171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129615 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37758" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129615 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129615 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/7e/7e979ac75636efa00cbc32ee92eff1a5fc1da3cea19378fbf5a39a5cc954ff45.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y={x}^{2}$ and lines $y=7x,$ $y=x+12,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129615 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d6b5334d-0ce9-5857-a701-46d283ab7257" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129615 #edb/ref 1074 "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/ee/ee6fd6a0b89a879d5803a98fda7e80a93926566995bea5f47a05aa7ab2986375.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 7x\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le x+12\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{7x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x+12}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129616 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186127177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129616 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37760" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129616 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129616 #edb/ref 1071 "${∬}_{|x|+|y|\\le 1}\\,\\,{e}^{x+y}\\,dA=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129616 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4267a45d-477c-5267-95c7-1da5f4e02116" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129616 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw a sketch of our region.\n\n![](images/4f/4f4e38950d36bf77ce4b2a907f07b3f9c4b40837729ef644f37ecfbd921aec8a.png)\n\n  \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/b8/b8075ab5905ada88b2a198f73738b2c0c507371cfea32b560c02be4f0185c92f.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,-x-1\\le y\\le x+1\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,x-1\\le y\\le -x+1\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{|x|+|y|\\le 1}{e}^{x+y}\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}{e}^{x+y}\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}{e}^{x+y}\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-1}^{x+1}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x-1}^{-x+1}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}[{e}^{x+y}]_{-x-1}^{x+1}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{e}^{x+y}]_{x-1}^{-x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}({e}^{2x+1}-{e}^{-1})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(e-{e}^{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{e}^{2x+1}}{2}-{e}^{-1}x]}_{-1}^{0}+{[ex-\\frac{{e}^{2x-1}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{e}{2}-(\\frac{{e}^{-1}}{2}+{e}^{-1})]+[(e-\\frac{e}{2})+\\frac{{e}^{-1}}{2}] \\\\  & =e-{e}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130075 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130075 #edb/ref 1061 26555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130075 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "677b9db4-978c-5d9a-9a29-29a0b08eb60b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130075 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130400 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130076 #edb/ref 1061 26556 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130076 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2f89bd90-2162-53d4-845f-4123449e769b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130076 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129192 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130077 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130077 #edb/ref 1061 26557 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130077 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "54b73f74-716d-5e9c-b4e0-441e927a08a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130077 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129193 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130078 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130078 #edb/ref 1061 26558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130078 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "91c2533d-2b41-5369-944b-c1f361a0d1ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130078 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130400 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we want to evaluate the double integral  \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} 2(x+y)\\,\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the finite region bounded by the lines $x=0, \\, y=1, \\, y=2, \\, y=3-x,$ and $y=x.$ How do we proceed?\n\nTo evaluate an integral like this, we carry out the following steps: \n\n**Step 1.** Sketch the region $D$. This allows us to determine the precise set-up of our integral. \n\nIn this example, we obtain the following:\n\n![](images/0a/0a90a4f377327f5293308f1e08ac6596f1c27b9bd47a614d6d7cb1c5dbfec33c.png)\n\n**Step 2.** Split (if necessary) the region $D$ into several type I or II regions.\n\nFrom the diagram above, we see that our region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as follows.\n\n![](images/a9/a93e1a0a0a7f9c104cb5d380b2a7ff98d6712ef0d2d67b74130da5dcf1701443.png)\n\n \n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x  \\leq 1, \\quad 1 \\leq y \\leq 2\\big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nD_2= \\{(x,y)\\: : \\: 1 \\leq x \\leq 3/2,  \\quad  x \\leq y \\leq 3-x\\}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** Set up and evaluate the integral using the additivity property of double integrals. We recall the following fact:\n\n*If $D$ is the union of two sub-regions, $D_1, D_2$, that don't overlap then,*\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A = \\iint\\limits_{D_1}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A + \\iint\\limits_{D_2}  f(x,y)\\ \\textrm d A.\n$$\n\nSo, finally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}2(x+y)\\text{ }dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{3/2}{\\int }_{x}^{3-x}2(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130400 #edb/ref 1065 4358 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130400 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ce229625-0660-5682-9e5a-3850f8ce33e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130400 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266170 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{55}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266170 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266170 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "02eb7e20-edcd-544d-a302-c240c7266269" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266562 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(