 [17592186394366 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394366 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=\\sqrt{x-2}+1,$ and the lines $y=2-\\frac{1}{2}x$ and $y=8-2x.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394366 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9fc12f5e-e89a-5d92-929e-151cd796ef36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394366 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=\\sqrt{x-2}+1 & \\,⟹\\,x=(y-1)^{2}+2 \\\\ y=2-\\frac{1}{2}x & \\,⟹\\,x=4-2y \\\\ y=8-2x & \\,⟹\\,x=4-\\frac{1}{2}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/3f/3f8e3ccfeac236d7fe9a502f599c61c404607a55ae809ec142019a3f881e1568.png)\n\n  \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/31/3148cb0f499564db9cbfd6b635fef81dc47298789241af4a243c32dbf4dc8247.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,4-2y\\le x\\le 4-\\frac{1}{2}y\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,(y-1)^{2}+2\\le x\\le 4-\\frac{1}{2}y\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{4-2y}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(y-1)^{2}+2}^{4-y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394367 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394367 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394367 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394367 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186394367 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394372 #edb/ref 17592